body:
@dario-piotrowicz  I get warnings for trying to animate stroke-dasharray. The animations work.
mdn says stroke-dasharray is animatable (https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/SVG/Attribute/stroke-dasharray)
Can I somehow disable the warning or am I actually doing something wrong?

```
animations: [
    trigger('wizardProgessAnimation', [

      state('*',
        style({ 'stroke-dasharray': '{{percentageParam}} 100' }),
        {params: { percentageParam: '0' }}
      ),

      transition(':enter', [
        animate('1s ease-out', keyframes([
          style({ 'stroke-dasharray': '{{percentageParam}} 100'})
        ]))
      ]),

      transition(':increment', [
        animate('1s ease-out', keyframes([
          style({ 'stroke-dasharray': '{{percentageParam}} 100'})
        ]))
      ]),

      transition(':decrement', [
        animate('1s ease-out', keyframes([
          style({ 'stroke-dasharray': '{{percentageParam}} 100'})
        ]))
      ]),

    ])
  ]


<path class="wizard-progress-circle" [@wizardProgessAnimation]="{value: percentage, params: {percentageParam: percentage}}"
        d="M18 2.0845
          a 15.9155 15.9155 0 0 1 0 31.831
          a 15.9155 15.9155 0 0 1 0 -31.831"
      />


.wizard-progress-circle {
  fill: none;
  stroke-width: 2.8;
  stroke-linecap: round;
}
```
